# Allowlist: the CLI image compiles the workspace and needs nothing else. See
# .devcontainer/Dockerfile.dockerignore for why this is a per-Dockerfile ignore
# file rather than a root .dockerignore.
#
# `cargo build -p rete-cli --locked` resolves against the workspace, so every
# member under crates/ has to be present even though only rete-cli and
# rete-core end up compiled. clients/ and fuzz/ are workspace-excluded and stay
# out.
**
!/Cargo.toml
!/Cargo.lock
!/rust-toolchain.toml
!/crates/**

# Never ship build output or fixtures-turned-artifacts into the context.
/crates/**/target
**/*.rete
